        "title": {
          "en": "A short story"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "The class collected the number of books read by 5 children: 4, 6, 5, 7, 8.\n\"What is the average?\" asked the teacher."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "mean",
          "mode",
          "range"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "Data are facts or numbers we collect. A tally helps us count. A pictograph shows data with pictures and a bar graph shows it with bars.\nThe mean or average is the sum divided by how many numbers. For 4, 6, 5, 7, 8 the sum is 30 and there are 5 numbers, so the mean is 6.\nThe mode is the number that occurs most often and the range is the greatest minus the least."
        }
      },
